Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?gpu:=20metal=20present=20=E2=80=94=20the=20real?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20fixes=20behind=20the=20white=20screen?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

the hunt for the blank window turned up five real defects, and the
present was rebuilt around what Metal provably renders:

- presentDrawable was missing before commit, so the compositor never
  saw a frame at all (the window stayed white while the game ran)
- the quads went into the vertex buffer in wrong-corner order; the
  six vertices now come from a per-draw 16-byte NDC rect bound with
  setVertexBytes, and screen_vertex synthesizes the (LT RT BR)(BR LB
  LT) corners from vertex_id itself. the old 72-float device-buffer
  fetch, perfect on paper, simply never rasterized
- the uv is oriented to the upload: row 0 is the top of the screen
- present.rs never forwarded set_top_width/set_layout/set_stereo/
  set_scaling to Metal, so the layout ran with top_width 1.0 and the
  top screen collapsed to three pixels wide; they are wired now
- the layer keeps framebufferOnly off: the screens get sampled, and
  M2.1's overlay will read it

the test pattern composes exactly: red top screen, blue bottom, navy
letterbox. test-pattern 120 frames at 60.2 fps.
